    "/api/integrations/transactions/batch": {
      "post": {
        "operationId": "ingest-batch",
        "summary": "Accept a finalized source batch atomically",
        "description": "transactions:write, active live key. One branch, 1\u201350 original source events using the finalized event contract. New financial events, numbering and all fees commit together or none commit.\n\nA failed batch returns 402 if the total fee for new eligible events exceeds available funds. Existing exact duplicates require no new fee. Any validation, authority, sequence or source conflict rejects the entire batch. Retain every unaccepted original on the client.\nBatches are limited to 10 requests/minute plus key admission budgets. These are protective limits, not measured throughput.\nClient preference can be realtime or batch. External POS/ERP connectors must implement the preference, durable source retention and bounded identical retries.",
        "tags": [
          "Merchant integration"
        ],
        "security": [
          {
            "MerchantKeyHeader": []
          },
          {
